    <briefdescription>
<para>Specify the number of cycles allowed after instruction issue before a particular use operand reads its registers. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This effectively reduces the write&apos;s latency. Here we allow negative cycles for corner cases where latency increases. This rule only applies when the entry&apos;s WriteResource matches the write&apos;s WriteResource.</para>
<para>MCReadAdvanceEntries are sorted first by operand index (UseIdx), then by WriteResourceIdx. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
